# CODEOWNERS — who must approve a change.
#
# SOC 2 (CM-3): with "Require review from Code Owners" enabled in the branch
# ruleset, GitHub refuses a merge until an owner of every touched path has
# approved. That turns "someone reviewed it" into "a senior reviewer looked at
# it", which is the separation of duties an auditor tests.
#
# One rule, deliberately. There is no per-area ownership here — path-specific
# owners only earn their complexity when different areas have genuinely
# different owners, and ours do not. A second rule would also be a footgun:
# the LAST matching line wins and matches do not accumulate, so a narrower rule
# added later silently replaces this one for those paths.
#
# The team is @zoneomics-dev/reviewers — Athar, with Nabeel and Saad as
# fallbacks. Any one of them satisfies the requirement; GitHub has no notion of
# a primary reviewer, so the ordering is a team convention, not a rule. Change
# the reviewer list by changing team membership, not this file.
#
# The team must hold write access in its own right. Members holding individual
# access is NOT enough — GitHub silently ignores the entry and the rule becomes
# unsatisfiable, with no error shown anywhere.

*                    @zoneomics-dev/reviewers

# Pinned last so a future narrower rule cannot quietly take ownership of the
# file that decides ownership. Redundant against the line above today, and kept
# deliberately.
/.github/CODEOWNERS  @zoneomics-dev/reviewers
